        "kind": "text",
        "text": "Level effect: anchor at August's 7.079 million. Momentum effect: carry only 25% of the recent average decline forward, a judgmental shrinkage weight reflecting noisy first prints and revisions. One-off effect: add zero separately and do not extrapolate April's concentrated jump, while retaining it in dispersion. Policy-mechanism effect: add zero because the fetched evidence supplies no calibrated independent policy contribution. Payroll evidence corroborates momentum without an additional adjustment."
