        "text": "Prior/update/interval: Use an August persistence prior of 7.079 million and the eight January-August original prints. Successive changes are [-0.064, -0.016, +0.752, -0.024, -0.235, -0.088, -0.192] million. Their mean is 0.019; summed squared deviations are 0.667738. Thus sigma = 0.333601 million = sqrt(0.667738 / (7 - 1)). Recent momentum is (-0.235 - 0.088 - 0.192) / 3 = -0.171667 million per month. Point = 7.079 + 0.25 * 2 * (-0.171667) + 0 one-off + 0 policy = 6.993167 million. The normal 80% monthly half-width is 1.28 * sigma = 0.427009 million. Two monthly innovations from August to October give half-width 0.427009 * sqrt(2) = 0.603882 million, a 1.414-fold horizon widening. Unrounded bounds are 6.389284 and 7.597049; rounding to thousand-job precision gives point 6.993 and interval [6.389, 7.597] million. Seven increments provide limited calibration, and April's jump materially influences the estimated dispersion."
